The most recent nethack fixes that were part of the 3.4.3 release have
not been included in Slashem yet.  Therefore, I noticed that the
loadstone item-duplication bug is still available for abuse.

With that in mind, I decided to try a PAIN ascension.  Along the way,
a few other conducts fell into place, so eventually I ascended with
what I call PPANICC-BUG conduct - pacifist, polyobjectless, atheist,
nude, illiterate, conflict-less, celibate, bag/box less, undying,
genocideless.

First move, I removed my cloak of MR.  Second move I dropped all my
weapon, armor, scrolls and spellbooks.  I found a wand of wishing on
level 4, before turn 300.

I only needed 94 wishes.

Artifacts
I needed MR, and I wouldn't be able to magic-map, so I picked the Eyes
of the Overworld. I wanted reflection while keeping my amulet slot
free, so I wielded Mirrorbright. I started eating amulets and rings to
get intrinsic MB, PfSC, and protection, then realized I should stay a
xorn the whole game. Half damage was a must, so I wished for the Orb
of Fate.  It also doubled for trap detection, and provided handy
levelports.

As I was leveling up, I realized that I had never looted or picked up
any container (box, bag, or chest).  With unlimited wishes, I figured
I would never need to.  My figurine of a Solar rapidly grew to level
49, so I never needed conflict to get it to attack anyone.  I wished
for some good armor for it.
Unfortunately, there were no weapon or armor shops in the entire
dungeon, otherwise it could have had some fully enchanted stuff.

The only non-coaligned priest in the whole main dungeon was in
Minetown.  I used a magic harp to boost my alignment enough to go on
the quest.

Occasionally, I would have to wield a potion of paralysis and whack a
teleporting monster,(i.e. WoY, Demogorgon) so that my Solar would have
a chance to finish it off.

